# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# 4.7 GB, and reproducible from the dependency list in the README.
.venv/

# --- Machine-specific configuration -----------------------------------------
# config.toml carries absolute paths to this machine's Steam library and save
# directory, which includes the Windows username. Copy config.example.toml to
# config.toml and point the three [game] paths at your own install.
config.toml

# --- Training artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# Checkpoints are large and regenerable: 29 policies plus the pixel students,
# which run to 135 MB each. metrics.jsonl is deliberately NOT ignored — it is
# only ~7 MB across every run and it is the evidence behind every number in the
# README, so a claim can be checked rather than taken on trust.
# `**` because captured frames sit a level deeper, in runs/<name>/frames/ —
# a runs/*/*.png pattern silently misses every one of them.
runs/**/*.pt
runs/**/*.png

# --- Phase 0 scratch --------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots taken while working out multi-instance launching, focus and
# capture. FINDINGS.md is the writeup and references none of them, so the
# conclusions survive without 5.8 MB of desktop captures.
spike/*.png
spike/capture-probe/

# --- Local game state -------------------------------------------------------
# Personal save backups taken before the frozen snapshot was cut. saves/ IS
# tracked: it is 76 KB and the pristine snapshot is required to reproduce a run.
backups/

# The game truncates this per launch and every instance shares it, so it is
# never reliable to diff anyway.
log.txt
*.log

# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store